  "title": "Erdős Problem #612",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $G$ be a connected graph with $n$ vertices, minimum degree $d$, and diameter $D$. Show if that $G$ contains no $K_{2r}$ and $(r-1)(3r+2)\\mid d$ then $ D\\leq \\frac{2(r-1)(3r+2)}{2r^2-1}\\frac{n}{d}+O(1), $ and if $G$ contains no $K_{2r+1}$ and $3r-1 \\mid d$ then $ D\\leq \\frac{3r-1}{r}\\frac{n}{d}+O(1). $ ",
